The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (tag_exists(name))
    n->item = get_item_from_tag(name);
```
Reason:
The logic incorrectly checks for the existence of a tag without considering that the root node (identified by the name "__root__") should directly reference the first item in the master list. This oversight leads to improper initialization of the root node's item, which can cause unexpected behavior or crashes.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!strcmp(name, "__root__"))
    n->item = list_first_entry_or_null(&menu.master, struct item, master);
else
    n->item = get_item_from_tag(name);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a specific check for the root node by comparing the name to "__root__". If it matches, it correctly initializes the root node's item to reference the first item in the master list, ensuring proper handling of this special case and preventing the previously encountered issues.

